---
// Instructions vs. data: trusted channels (system, user) carry authority over the agent; untrusted external content is wrapped in a source tag before entering the context, and the context layer is only the first line of defense.
---

<svg
	class="dg"
	viewBox="0 0 720 522"
	role="img"
	aria-labelledby="d2-idb-title d2-idb-desc"
	style="min-width: 630px"
>
	<title id="d2-idb-title">Separating instructions from data</title>
	<desc id="d2-idb-desc">
		Left: trusted channels, the system prompt and the user's direct request, sent in their own Chat Template roles.
		Right: untrusted external content, each item wrapped in an external_content tag that annotates its source: web
		page hidden text, email, PDF metadata, image EXIF metadata, a third-party Skill, and a status-bar source an
		attacker can manipulate. Both flow into the context, the trusted channels through structured roles and the
		external content through input sanitization, which is auxiliary only. In the context, instructions carry
		authority and data is only material to be processed. A banner notes that the context layer is only the first line
		of defense; the execution and data layers are in lesson 1.8 and later chapters.
	</desc>
	<defs>
		<marker id="d2-idb-arrow" viewBox="0 0 10 10" refX="9" refY="5" markerWidth="8" markerHeight="8" orient="auto-start-reverse">
			<path d="M0,0 L10,5 L0,10 z" class="dg-arrowhead"></path>
		</marker>
	</defs>

	<text x="2" y="28" class="dg-title">Separating instructions from data</text>

	<!-- Left: trusted channels -->
	<g class="dg-container dg-harness">
		<rect x="2" y="44" width="220" height="258" rx="12"></rect>
		<text x="14" y="72" font-weight="700">Trusted channels</text>
		<text x="14" y="94" class="dg-sub">may direct behavior</text>
	</g>
	<g class="dg-node dg-harness">
		<rect x="14" y="118" width="196" height="64" rx="8"></rect>
		<text x="30" y="143" class="dg-accent" font-weight="700">system</text>
		<text x="30" y="167" class="dg-sub">system prompt</text>
	</g>
	<g class="dg-node dg-harness">
		<rect x="14" y="206" width="196" height="64" rx="8"></rect>
		<text x="30" y="231" class="dg-accent" font-weight="700">user</text>
		<text x="30" y="255" class="dg-sub">direct user request</text>
	</g>

	<!-- Right: untrusted content, wrapped in source tags -->
	<g class="dg-container dg-guard">
		<rect x="246" y="44" width="472" height="258" rx="12"></rect>
		<text x="258" y="72" font-weight="700">&lt;external_content source="…"&gt;</text>
		<text x="258" y="94" class="dg-sub">untrusted: material, not instructions</text>
	</g>
	<g class="dg-node dg-env">
		<rect x="258" y="110" width="220" height="48" rx="8"></rect>
		<text x="274" y="140">Web page hidden text</text>
	</g>
	<g class="dg-node dg-env">
		<rect x="490" y="110" width="216" height="48" rx="8"></rect>
		<text x="506" y="140">Email</text>
	</g>
	<g class="dg-node dg-env">
		<rect x="258" y="170" width="220" height="48" rx="8"></rect>
		<text x="274" y="200">PDF metadata</text>
	</g>
	<g class="dg-node dg-env">
		<rect x="490" y="170" width="216" height="48" rx="8"></rect>
		<text x="506" y="200">Image EXIF metadata</text>
	</g>
	<g class="dg-node dg-env">
		<rect x="258" y="230" width="220" height="48" rx="8"></rect>
		<text x="274" y="260">Third-party Skill</text>
	</g>
	<g class="dg-node dg-env">
		<rect x="490" y="230" width="216" height="48" rx="8"></rect>
		<text x="506" y="260">Status-bar source</text>
	</g>

	<!-- Context -->
	<g class="dg-node dg-context">
		<rect x="2" y="356" width="716" height="72" rx="10"></rect>
		<text x="18" y="384" class="dg-accent" font-weight="700">Context</text>
		<text x="18" y="410" class="dg-sub">instructions carry authority; data is only material to be processed</text>
	</g>

	<g class="dg-edge">
		<line x1="112" y1="302" x2="112" y2="354" marker-end="url(#d2-idb-arrow)"></line>
		<text x="124" y="334" class="dg-edge-label">structured roles</text>
	</g>
	<g class="dg-edge">
		<line x1="482" y1="302" x2="482" y2="354" marker-end="url(#d2-idb-arrow)"></line>
		<text x="494" y="334" class="dg-edge-label">input sanitization (auxiliary)</text>
	</g>

	<!-- Banner -->
	<g class="dg-node dg-neutral">
		<rect x="2" y="446" width="716" height="72" rx="10"></rect>
		<text x="18" y="474" font-weight="700">Context layer = first line of defense only</text>
		<text x="18" y="500" class="dg-sub">Execution and data layers: lesson 1.8 and later chapters</text>
	</g>
</svg>
